  "Define the industry before rating forces: Indonesian consumer grocery retail, including traditional and online sellers. Hypermart supplied about 85% of MPPA revenue in 2020. David Chapter 3, printed pp. 101–104, and the Harvard Business School Five Forces page provide the method. Our assessment: rivalry high; buyer power and entry threat moderate; meal substitution moderate; merchandise supplier power low–moderate. Cross-check Alfamidi pp. 71 and 140, Ranch pp. 80 and 134 and financial-statement Notes 24–25, Hero pp. 92–93, Indoritel pp. 24 and 67–68, and Nielsen’s April 2020 consumer research (fieldwork 7–10 March). The framework concerns competitive structure and profitability, not a measured allocation of MPPA’s sales decline. Case sources: printed pp. 590–594. MPPA AR2020 Notes 23–24, PDF p. 246.": "Tentukan industri sebelum menilai kekuatan: ritel pangan konsumen Indonesia, termasuk penjual tradisional dan daring. Hypermart menyumbang sekitar 85% pendapatan MPPA pada 2020. Metode mengacu David Bab 3 hlm. 101–104 dan laman Lima Kekuatan Harvard Business School. Penilaian kita: persaingan tinggi; daya tawar pembeli dan ancaman masuk sedang; penggantian untuk belanja makanan sedang; daya tawar pemasok barang dagangan rendah–sedang. Periksa Alfamidi hlm. 71 dan 140, Ranch hlm. 80 dan 134 serta Catatan 24–25, Hero hlm. 92–93, Indoritel hlm. 24 dan 67–68, serta riset Nielsen April 2020 (survei 7–10 Maret). Model membahas struktur persaingan dan laba, bukan pembagian terukur penyebab penurunan penjualan MPPA. Sumber kasus: hlm. 590–594; AR2020 MPPA Catatan 23–24, PDF hlm. 246."
